{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b6h7f1f0o","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kg6roKqTm6hARcT6JxoNAj","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run2-repo/5c9ca1dc-60bc-49fa-b995-f321aedbe2b5/tasks/b6h7f1f0o.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_5\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of `motif_stack`: people judge randomness as the likelihood ratio of a fair coin against Griffiths et al.'s four-motif stack automaton (shared by everyone), but individuals differ in how strongly they additionally treat frequent alternation itself as a sign of randomness. The one change is a person-specific alternation-preference weight (drawn from a population distribution) on the difference in alternation rate between the two sequences, addressing the critique that the data show far more individual variation in alternation preference than a single-population model produces.\nEOF\necho motif_stack_person_alternation > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc = open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/models/motif_stack.py\").read()\nD=\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_5\"\n# docstring\nstart = src.index('\"\"\"', 3) + 3\ndoc = '''\"\"\"Refinement of motif_stack: the four-motif stack automaton plus person-specific\nalternation preference.\n\nHypothesis: people judge randomness as the log-likelihood ratio of a fair coin\nagainst Griffiths et al. (2018)'s four-motif stack automaton (shared by\neveryone), but individuals differ in how strongly they additionally treat\nfrequent alternation itself as a sign of randomness. The single change from\nmotif_stack is a person-specific weight (non-centred population distribution,\n400 slots so new participants are draws from it) on the difference in\nalternation rate between the two sequences.\n\"\"\"'''\nsrc = doc + src[start:]\nsrc = src.replace('''    return {\n        **_unique_sequence_table(sequences),''', '''    participant_id = np.array(\n        [int(float(row[\"participant_id\"])) for row in rows], dtype=\"int64\"\n    )\n    if participant_id.min() < 0 or participant_id.max() >= N_PARTICIPANT_SLOTS:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"participant_id outside [0, {N_PARTICIPANT_SLOTS}): \"\n            f\"{participant_id.min()}..{participant_id.max()}\"\n        )\n    alt_diff = np.array(\n        [_alternation_rate(a) - _alternation_rate(b) for a, b in zip(sequences_a, sequences_b)],\n        dtype=\"float64\",\n    )\n\n    return {\n        **_unique_sequence_table(sequences),\n        \"participant_id\": participant_id,\n        \"alt_diff\": alt_diff,''')\nsrc = src.replace('''def _memory_flags''', '''def _alternation_rate(seq: str) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Share of adjacent flips that differ.\"\"\"\n    if len(seq) < 2:\n        return 0.0\n    return sum(1 for x, y in zip(seq, seq[1:]) if x != y) / (len(seq) - 1)\n\n\ndef _memory_flags''')\nsrc = src.replace('N_STATES = 6\\n', 'N_STATES = 6\\nN_PARTICIPANT_SLOTS = 400\\n')\nsrc = src.replace('_PLACEHOLDER = prepare_observed([{\"sequence_a\": \"HT\", \"sequence_b\": \"HT\"}])',\n '_PLACEHOLDER = prepare_observed(\\n    [{\"sequence_a\": \"HT\", \"sequence_b\": \"HT\", \"participant_id\": 0}]\\n)')\nsrc = src.replace('''    chose_left = pm.Data(\"chose_left\", _PLACEHOLDER[\"chose_left\"])\n''', '''    chose_left = pm.Data(\"chose_left\", _PLACEHOLDER[\"chose_left\"])\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\", _PLACEHOLDER[\"participant_id\"])\n    alt_diff = pm.Data(\"alt_diff\", _PLACEHOLDER[\"alt_diff\"])\n''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    side_bias = pm.Uniform(\"side_bias\", lower=-2.0, upper=2.0)\n''', '''    side_bias = pm.Uniform(\"side_bias\", lower=-2.0, upper=2.0)\n\n    # Person-specific alternation preference (non-centred).\n    alt_mu = pm.Normal(\"alt_mu\", mu=0.0, sigma=2.0)\n    alt_sigma = pm.HalfNormal(\"alt_sigma\", sigma=1.5)\n    alt_z = pm.Normal(\"alt_z\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=N_PARTICIPANT_SLOTS)\n    alt_weight = alt_mu + alt_sigma * alt_z\n''')\nsrc = src.replace('''pm.math.sigmoid(beta * (score[idx_a] - score[idx_b]) + side_bias),''',\n'''pm.math.sigmoid(\n            beta * (score[idx_a] - score[idx_b])\n            + alt_weight[participant_id] * alt_diff\n            + side_bias\n        ),''')\nassert src.count(\"alt_weight[participant_id]\")==1 and '\"alt_diff\": alt_diff' in src\nopen(D+\"/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && time /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses $D/../../responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -15\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"df3fb804-569b-4343-b8f0-fb77fcd2c53b","session_id":"5c9ca1dc-60bc-49fa-b995-f321aedbe2b5"}
